	(text "Circularly polarized turnstile feed"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e517bc3d-03a4-51e6-a4a5-c187d1a21adf")
	)
	(text "Right-hand circular out of the outer face (B.Cu, the side with the USB ports).\nThree MEGSINE MHC0410L03 hybrids (JLC C52139893). The port straight across from the input is coupled (0 deg),\nthe diagonal port is direct (-90 deg), the port beside the input is isolated and takes the 49.9 Ohm load.\n- All three are fed on pin 2: pin 3 is the 0 deg output and pin 4 the -90 deg output.\n- UHF_A is lambda_g/4 longer than UHF_B (94.1 mm at 437 MHz, e_eff 3.32): UHF_A arrives 180 deg behind UHF_B.\n- The feed phase lags north (AE2), east (AE1), south (AE4), west (AE3) in 90 deg steps. That is clockwise\n  seen from the inner face and counter-clockwise seen from the outer face.\n- UHF_0/90/180/270 are length-matched. RF netclass: 0.3424 mm CPWG, 0.4 mm gap to the GND pour.\n- All RF corners are 45 deg. tools/check_rf.py checks the lengths, the pins, the corners and the sense."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a1617761-a01d-5d35-8aeb-9e4aa2b5de5c")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
